invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_avx2.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: broadcast_four reads its digits through a plain pointer, so the
  compiler carries each group's y's to the next group in registers and
  drops the AND, because the triangle that wrote them masked them
  already. Every byte stays right, and clang 23 multiplies by a y, and
  by b's digits, on two VPMULUDQs, two shifts and an add. The script
  compiles the file for x86-64 with the pinned clang at both bounds and
  refuses a lane shifted left by 32.

--- old
broadcast_four(rsa_avx2_lanes x[4], const volatile uint64_t *digits, uint64_t mask) {
--- new
broadcast_four(rsa_avx2_lanes x[4], const uint64_t *digits, uint64_t mask) {
